WEBVTT

00:35.201 --> 00:36.536
I…

00:39.497 --> 00:41.124
passed the interview.

00:57.348 --> 00:58.266
Rin.

00:59.851 --> 01:00.894
Congratulations.

01:02.062 --> 01:05.023
You really earned it.

01:15.241 --> 01:16.326
Thank you.

01:27.545 --> 01:29.547
I know that I

01:31.341 --> 01:33.426
put you in a tough spot…

01:35.637 --> 01:38.056
and that you thought
really hard about it for me.

01:40.517 --> 01:41.935
I know it all.

01:46.314 --> 01:47.649
So…

01:49.692 --> 01:54.447
I want to treasure that no matter…

01:56.449 --> 01:57.951
what happens.

02:00.078 --> 02:01.454
I want to keep it safe with me…

02:05.834 --> 02:07.293
even when I return to Korea.

02:20.890 --> 02:23.518
If you feel lonely, don't hide it.

02:25.311 --> 02:26.312
Okay.

02:27.230 --> 02:28.398
You too.

02:28.481 --> 02:30.233
I never hide it.

02:31.025 --> 02:32.110
You know that, don't you?

02:33.194 --> 02:34.154
That's true.

02:46.082 --> 02:47.375
We will…

02:48.960 --> 02:50.086
be okay.

02:53.756 --> 02:54.591
Yeah.

04:03.868 --> 04:06.037
CLOSED FOR PRIVATE EVENT

04:06.120 --> 04:07.413
Picture time!

04:07.497 --> 04:09.374
Hurry, hurry! Come on!

04:10.291 --> 04:12.627
Closer, closer. Okay.

04:12.710 --> 04:14.295
Okay, say

04:14.379 --> 04:17.298
-Tanomi!
-Tanomi!

04:22.929 --> 04:27.141
Actually, having a takoyaki party was
on my bucket list too.

04:27.725 --> 04:29.477
-Really?
-Yeah.

04:29.560 --> 04:31.312
-I'm glad we got to do it together.
-Yeah.

04:31.396 --> 04:32.772
Thanks.

04:32.855 --> 04:35.400
They're turning perfectly round.

04:35.483 --> 04:36.317
Yeah.

04:36.401 --> 04:37.527
This one's burning.

04:37.610 --> 04:38.611
Ouch!

04:39.279 --> 04:40.321
That was hot.

04:41.447 --> 04:42.782
Of course it's hot.

04:42.865 --> 04:44.784
-It was my bare hand, too.
-No wonder.

04:49.414 --> 04:50.665
Thank you.

04:57.005 --> 04:58.673
The last time we met…

05:01.217 --> 05:04.095
I'm sorry I was rude to you.

05:04.929 --> 05:06.723
Oh no, it's nothing.

05:08.891 --> 05:13.229
-You see, I told you it's hot!
-It's so hot!

05:13.813 --> 05:15.398
Are you okay?

05:15.481 --> 05:17.358
Shige, I want to eat one too.

05:17.442 --> 05:18.276
Sure.

05:18.359 --> 05:20.069
-This one?
-Rin

05:20.153 --> 05:22.071
-needed you, it seems.
-Try this one.

05:26.868 --> 05:30.621
Please take care of Rin from now on too.

05:36.753 --> 05:39.255
Yes, I will.

05:40.298 --> 05:42.383
-Jjan.
-Jjan.

05:45.136 --> 05:46.888
‎Rin, that one is ready to eat.

05:46.971 --> 05:48.014
Here, Shige.

05:48.097 --> 05:49.223
Thank you.

05:50.975 --> 05:52.977
So when are you going back?

05:54.645 --> 05:57.565
The 28th.

05:58.191 --> 05:59.734
That's so soon!

06:02.612 --> 06:03.988
I see…

06:05.406 --> 06:07.033
It'll be lonely without you.

06:13.581 --> 06:14.457
Sorry.

06:17.794 --> 06:19.003
It's okay.

06:19.087 --> 06:21.464
I'm just going to be
a little far away, that's all.

06:22.048 --> 06:24.092
Nothing else will change.

06:24.175 --> 06:27.970
I mean, we have social media
and video calling too.

06:28.054 --> 06:29.138
Yeah.

06:29.222 --> 06:32.141
Nothing will change between us.

06:34.143 --> 06:35.853
You two will be okay.

06:36.604 --> 06:38.689
If you love each other,

06:38.773 --> 06:41.109
it'll be okay no matter where you are.

06:41.192 --> 06:42.318
Right?

06:43.111 --> 06:44.362
Shige…

06:44.862 --> 06:45.696
Hey,

06:45.780 --> 06:47.949
I bet you think
those were such wise words.

06:48.032 --> 06:49.033
I do.

06:50.201 --> 06:53.538
And so, Rin, come visit us anytime.

06:53.621 --> 06:57.333
When you feel lonely,
you just need to come visit… me.

06:59.085 --> 07:00.294
I will.

07:01.170 --> 07:03.005
-You heard that?
-Oh, Shige…

07:13.724 --> 07:15.935
-Taiga.
-Yes?

07:17.854 --> 07:19.564
I'll give this to you.

07:20.648 --> 07:21.524
What?

07:37.874 --> 07:41.252
-This is… yours.
-Yeah.

07:42.753 --> 07:44.046
Make sure you sharpen it.

07:45.548 --> 07:49.385
Pay more attention to how you sharpen
your knife than how you cut with it.

07:54.223 --> 07:57.101
Yes. I will use it with the utmost care.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.984
Thank you very much.

08:10.281 --> 08:12.533
-Um, Shige…
-Huh?

08:13.826 --> 08:15.328
If it's not too much trouble,

08:15.870 --> 08:18.748
may I continue working here
even when I start school?

08:18.831 --> 08:21.834
Well, I appreciate that you want to,

08:22.376 --> 08:23.961
but shouldn't you focus on school?

08:25.880 --> 08:29.342
Tanomi is where my roots are.

08:30.051 --> 08:34.013
Thanks to you, Shige, and our customers,

08:35.723 --> 08:37.475
I am who I am today.

08:38.142 --> 08:40.937
That's why I want to continue helping out

08:41.020 --> 08:42.939
for as long as I can.

08:52.490 --> 08:55.243
Well then,
maybe I will take you up on that offer.

08:57.036 --> 08:59.622
Okay. Thank you very much.

09:00.456 --> 09:01.290
TANOMI

09:01.374 --> 09:02.542
HERE ARE THE PHOTOS FROM TODAY! THANK YOU!

09:50.256 --> 09:52.008
It's already been a year, huh?

10:24.415 --> 10:25.708
Hello?

10:26.334 --> 10:28.210
I'm sorry. Were you sleeping?

10:28.794 --> 10:30.004
No.

10:30.796 --> 10:32.006
What's up?

10:33.507 --> 10:34.508
You know…

10:36.260 --> 10:38.054
There's a place I want to take you.

10:41.641 --> 10:44.060
So this is where you grew up?

10:46.103 --> 10:49.440
It's a comfortable and warm place,

10:49.523 --> 10:50.691
just like you.

10:51.317 --> 10:52.485
Really?

10:55.029 --> 10:58.366
It feels strange to be here with you.

10:59.950 --> 11:02.536
I was always practicing on my own.

11:03.162 --> 11:05.498
I would use this as my starting line,

11:06.666 --> 11:08.459
and run downstream.

11:11.212 --> 11:13.589
I loved running here.

11:14.882 --> 11:17.843
The wind, the sounds, the scents…

11:19.762 --> 11:21.680
Everything felt amazing.

11:23.140 --> 11:26.310
-I want to see you running.
-What?

11:26.977 --> 11:28.062
That's embarrassing.

11:28.145 --> 11:30.106
Come on. Just once.

11:30.189 --> 11:32.983
Okay, let's race to that point.

11:33.067 --> 11:34.443
There's no way you'd win.

11:34.527 --> 11:35.820
Sijag!

11:39.782 --> 11:40.825
You're serious?

11:48.707 --> 11:49.583
Taiga!

11:51.710 --> 11:52.753
Wait…

12:17.319 --> 12:18.279
Rin?

12:26.954 --> 12:28.080
What's wrong?

12:30.082 --> 12:31.125
I'm sorry.

12:32.376 --> 12:34.920
But you were going so far away…

13:28.182 --> 13:30.518
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

13:45.533 --> 13:48.827
Taiga is always taking care of me.

13:49.537 --> 13:51.372
My name is Park Rin.

13:55.167 --> 13:57.836
Oh, this is…

13:58.629 --> 14:01.340
no… um…

14:02.299 --> 14:06.011
It's nothing much, but please enjoy.

14:06.095 --> 14:07.388
Oh my.

14:07.471 --> 14:10.182
You didn't have to. Thank you.

14:11.725 --> 14:14.228
Rin is from Korea,

14:14.311 --> 14:16.230
and came here to study animation.

14:17.565 --> 14:21.527
So you're going to work
in the animation field in Japan?

14:27.575 --> 14:28.742
No.

14:29.535 --> 14:33.372
Once I graduate,
I plan on working in Korea,

14:33.455 --> 14:35.291
designing for an advertising company.

14:36.166 --> 14:37.084
I see…

14:37.585 --> 14:39.211
Is that right?

14:40.671 --> 14:43.674
So when are you graduating?

14:47.303 --> 14:49.305
-This month.
-What?

14:50.848 --> 14:54.894
So this month you're going back to Korea?

14:58.856 --> 14:59.899
Yes.

15:03.819 --> 15:05.154
Um…

15:06.322 --> 15:07.531
You two are dating, right?

15:09.033 --> 15:11.243
Yes, we are.

15:20.085 --> 15:23.422
I'm sorry for making you worried.

15:24.089 --> 15:27.551
But we made this decision together.

15:29.803 --> 15:31.180
We came here

15:32.348 --> 15:34.850
because I wanted to show Rin
the place where I grew up.

15:38.854 --> 15:39.897
I…

15:41.815 --> 15:46.070
have a goal now, thanks to Rin.

15:48.280 --> 15:49.323
The truth is,

15:50.532 --> 15:52.910
I'm thinking of becoming
a registered dietitian.

15:53.869 --> 15:54.912
So…

15:56.163 --> 15:57.873
I'm going to school starting April.

15:58.499 --> 15:59.750
Wait a second.

16:01.251 --> 16:02.586
You're going back to school?

16:02.670 --> 16:05.255
But what about the restaurant?

16:06.674 --> 16:08.592
The owner was very understanding,

16:09.301 --> 16:11.387
so I'm going to work
while going to school.

16:11.470 --> 16:13.222
That's not realistic.

16:13.806 --> 16:15.182
What if it doesn't work again--

16:15.265 --> 16:16.934
Even if it doesn't work, again,

16:18.018 --> 16:19.103
I'll be fine this time.

16:21.647 --> 16:25.192
Because now I know that
I can always start again.

16:40.624 --> 16:43.085
RENEWS HIGHEST RANKING

16:51.593 --> 16:52.594
Taiga.

16:53.262 --> 16:54.555
You're okay on time?

17:00.185 --> 17:05.149
I was just thinking about
how hard I worked back then.

17:16.201 --> 17:18.704
Thank you for having me today.

17:18.787 --> 17:19.747
My pleasure.

17:21.498 --> 17:23.000
Next time…

17:29.006 --> 17:29.840
See you.

17:32.134 --> 17:33.010
Wait.

17:39.975 --> 17:42.686
Send me the address
of the place you're working at.

17:44.772 --> 17:45.731
What?

17:46.774 --> 17:48.484
They're taking care of you, right?

17:49.902 --> 17:51.278
When I go to Tokyo,

17:52.696 --> 17:53.822
I'll pay my respects.

18:01.455 --> 18:02.581
Okay.

18:04.500 --> 18:07.044
Thank you, Big Bro.

18:17.137 --> 18:21.725
When Taiga decided to quit track,

18:22.935 --> 18:25.479
I was anxious and worried,

18:25.562 --> 18:27.606
so I said a lot
of unnecessary things to him.

18:28.565 --> 18:32.945
That has always been bothering me.

18:36.240 --> 18:40.035
I realized
that I should've had more faith in him,

18:40.119 --> 18:42.287
and let him follow his own course.

18:43.122 --> 18:45.833
Seeing him today made me realize that.

18:47.167 --> 18:48.794
You and Taiga

18:48.877 --> 18:51.380
will be able to find
what is best for the both of you.

18:53.006 --> 18:54.466
I am sure.

18:56.718 --> 18:57.678
Yes.

19:02.683 --> 19:05.644
Mom, we'll have to leave soon.

19:06.228 --> 19:07.896
-Take care, you two.
-Thanks.

19:08.438 --> 19:11.275
Rin, please take care of Taiga.

19:11.942 --> 19:14.695
Oh, he is always the one
taking care of me.

19:25.956 --> 19:26.832
I…

19:27.624 --> 19:29.710
will do my best, one step at a time.

19:36.175 --> 19:37.426
I'm looking forward to it.

19:39.469 --> 19:41.096
But don't overwork yourself.

20:01.658 --> 20:05.454
GRADUATION EXHIBITION

20:07.539 --> 20:09.958
TOKYO UNIVERSITY OF FINE ARTS
DEPARTMENT OF ANIMATION

20:10.042 --> 20:13.253
ONIGIRI - PARK RIN

20:13.337 --> 20:15.005
Back when I first started school,

20:16.006 --> 20:18.425
I wanted to become an animator,

20:19.051 --> 20:22.221
but I didn't have anything
specific in mind.

20:27.184 --> 20:29.478
What do I want to do?

20:29.561 --> 20:31.188
What am I capable of?

20:31.772 --> 20:36.109
I didn't know the answer
and was completely lost.

20:49.957 --> 20:51.541
Thinking back now,

20:52.668 --> 20:54.878
there were moments
I compared myself to others…

20:57.673 --> 21:00.467
and moments where I suffered
from self-doubt.

21:00.550 --> 21:02.344
But all of those moments…

21:06.974 --> 21:11.853
were very important detours
that I had to make, in a way.

21:14.815 --> 21:17.234
Just to make one onigiri,

21:17.818 --> 21:21.029
you need to cook the rice,
prepare the stuffing,

21:21.530 --> 21:22.572
and wrap it in seaweed.

21:36.420 --> 21:39.631
Everything is a product
of small, individual steps.

21:44.803 --> 21:48.140
And what's important
is what kind of outlook

21:48.223 --> 21:51.268
you have on each and every one
of those steps.

21:56.231 --> 21:59.651
That is what I learned
over the past two years.

22:28.263 --> 22:31.016
I hope that this animation

22:31.641 --> 22:34.269
motivates you to cast a spotlight

22:34.895 --> 22:37.272
on fleeting moments like these.

22:38.815 --> 22:42.694
Thank you very much for watching.

23:02.547 --> 23:06.176
Mom, I just returned the key.

23:08.595 --> 23:10.555
I'll head to the airport soon.

23:43.463 --> 23:44.506
Shall we go?

23:47.342 --> 23:48.260
Yeah.

24:12.993 --> 24:17.497
NARITA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

24:26.631 --> 24:31.178
All right, so we'll send a message
every day when we wake up,

24:31.261 --> 24:33.096
and we'll do a video call before bed.

24:33.180 --> 24:34.514
These two are a must, right?

24:34.598 --> 24:35.432
Yeah.

24:35.515 --> 24:38.977
As soon as I can take time off,
I'll send you my schedule.

24:40.312 --> 24:44.691
I think I can visit you
some time during summer break too.

24:47.569 --> 24:48.695
Well then…

24:53.116 --> 24:54.326
I guess…

24:57.329 --> 24:58.914
we're all set?

25:09.216 --> 25:10.175
Oh, that's right.

25:11.801 --> 25:12.844
One final thing…

25:13.678 --> 25:16.014
I mean, it's not "final" but…

25:18.558 --> 25:21.853
I wanted you to eat this.

25:39.746 --> 25:40.872
Thank you.

25:42.332 --> 25:43.333
I'm so happy.

25:53.969 --> 25:55.178
Thanks.

26:11.444 --> 26:14.990
What is this called?

26:21.288 --> 26:25.458
It's shigure-ni
with shishito peppers and beef.

26:26.918 --> 26:28.169
Shigure-ni…

26:30.547 --> 26:34.009
It kind of tastes like Korean jang-jorim.

26:48.273 --> 26:50.859
I'm sorry, we're closed for today.

26:50.942 --> 26:52.986
TANOMI

26:53.069 --> 26:54.696
Okay…

26:54.779 --> 26:58.283
-You eat like you really enjoy the food.
-Joesongham-- I mean, I'm sorry.

27:00.702 --> 27:03.204
Out of all the onigiri I've had in Japan,

27:03.288 --> 27:04.664
this is the best.

27:08.043 --> 27:09.210
The Classic.

27:09.836 --> 27:13.340
This is like a scene
out of my favorite movie.

27:19.137 --> 27:21.014
-Bucket list?
-Yes.

27:21.723 --> 27:24.184
Why don't you make one too?

27:24.267 --> 27:25.602
When I'm with you,

27:26.353 --> 27:29.647
I feel like I can move forward.

27:34.152 --> 27:37.822
Taiga, are you not that good
at keeping in touch?

27:39.407 --> 27:42.285
When you don't read my messages,

27:42.369 --> 27:44.788
or a day goes by without a word from you,

27:44.871 --> 27:47.540
I start to wonder
if you have no interest in me.

27:48.208 --> 27:49.751
Happy birthday!

27:51.628 --> 27:53.630
Why didn't you say anything?

27:54.672 --> 27:55.673
Whatever.

27:57.634 --> 27:59.219
Maybe it is difficult for two people

28:00.136 --> 28:02.514
from different backgrounds to be together?

28:02.597 --> 28:04.265
From now on…

28:04.349 --> 28:06.893
I want to know more about

28:07.560 --> 28:08.853
the things you value.

28:09.896 --> 28:10.939
Thank you.

28:12.941 --> 28:14.401
I believe

28:14.484 --> 28:17.153
that your training right now
will not be wasted.

28:17.237 --> 28:19.572
Just like you said,

28:20.323 --> 28:24.828
if we try our best to share
everything with each other,

28:25.912 --> 28:28.915
we won't be lonely
even if we're far apart…

28:30.208 --> 28:31.292
I think.

28:31.376 --> 28:32.961
Why didn't you tell me?

28:33.920 --> 28:34.838
Well…

28:35.713 --> 28:36.840
Were you hiding it?

28:37.507 --> 28:39.050
Of course not.

28:39.134 --> 28:42.303
I wish you would've accepted me,
even just for a second.

28:43.596 --> 28:45.932
Why don't you get it?

28:49.519 --> 28:50.478
Sorry.

28:51.646 --> 28:52.814
I can't keep up with you.

29:05.994 --> 29:07.287
Your words…

29:08.121 --> 29:09.330
Your smile…

29:09.998 --> 29:11.207
Everything about you

29:11.958 --> 29:13.501
gave me strength.

29:15.920 --> 29:17.881
I don't want to let you go yet.

29:19.466 --> 29:21.676
Whether I'm feeling happy, or anything,

29:21.760 --> 29:22.969
‎FORTUNE

29:23.052 --> 29:25.263
the first person I think of is you.

29:26.639 --> 29:28.725
Everything brings me back to you.

29:30.435 --> 29:32.020
I like you, Taiga.

29:33.229 --> 29:36.941
I want to stay with you
even after you graduate.

29:40.069 --> 29:43.156
I want to be with you too.

29:52.749 --> 29:53.708
Rin…

29:55.376 --> 29:58.463
You can't stay here, right?

30:03.301 --> 30:04.177
I'm sorry.

30:05.303 --> 30:06.805
I didn't want to end things like this…

30:06.888 --> 30:07.722
I mean,

30:08.973 --> 30:10.558
I know it's not the end, but…

30:12.143 --> 30:13.269
But you know…

30:16.105 --> 30:17.106
I was…

30:24.072 --> 30:25.490
saved by you.

30:28.368 --> 30:29.410
Taiga…

30:39.629 --> 30:40.672
Thank you.

30:42.423 --> 30:43.842
Thank you so much.

31:50.408 --> 31:51.492
Hello?

31:51.576 --> 31:52.660
Hello.

31:52.744 --> 31:54.412
-Did you eat already?
-Yeah.

31:54.495 --> 31:55.413
What about you?

31:55.496 --> 31:56.372
I ate.

31:56.915 --> 31:58.124
How was your presentation?

31:59.292 --> 32:00.126
It went well.

32:00.710 --> 32:02.795
Did you finish your assignment on time?

32:02.879 --> 32:04.255
I barely made it.

32:04.339 --> 32:05.381
I'm glad.

32:06.215 --> 32:07.342
Good work.

32:08.384 --> 32:09.886
You too.

32:12.805 --> 32:14.933
-Jjan.
-Jjan.

32:27.070 --> 32:30.323
I CAN'T WAIT TO SEE YOU

32:36.537 --> 32:38.081
Happy birthday!

32:38.873 --> 32:40.124
Rin!

32:42.168 --> 32:44.712
-Thank you!
-Congratulations.

32:44.796 --> 32:46.506
I missed you.

32:56.766 --> 33:00.979
The smell comes from the oil
in between the skin and flesh.

33:01.062 --> 33:04.524
If you cook it from the skin side first,
it starts to come out.

33:04.607 --> 33:09.487
As the oil comes out, keep removing it
using something like a paper towel.

33:09.570 --> 33:12.615
By doing this,
you can get rid of that smell…

33:26.129 --> 33:28.297
TAIGA: ARE YOU GOING ANYWHERE THIS SUMMER?

33:32.969 --> 33:34.095
Let's go.

33:34.178 --> 33:36.097
What should we get? Beer?

33:37.682 --> 33:39.350
-Sounds good.
-Come on!

34:01.414 --> 34:03.249
‎VISITING A CAFE WITH A FRIEND

34:12.467 --> 34:13.384
Excuse me.

34:14.469 --> 34:15.470
Welcome.

34:56.219 --> 34:57.762
Here's this month's payment.

34:59.597 --> 35:00.765
Thank you.

35:01.390 --> 35:02.391
Okay.

35:04.894 --> 35:06.270
By the way, I read it.

35:06.354 --> 35:07.855
Akki's Pachiizm.

35:10.233 --> 35:11.442
Congrats on your first serialization.

35:12.068 --> 35:14.153
-You're amazing, Dongsaeng!
-No, I'm not.

35:14.237 --> 35:16.447
It took me two whole years!

35:16.531 --> 35:18.324
Being a writer is really tough.

35:22.745 --> 35:24.872
Hyeongnim, can I take this real quick?

35:26.457 --> 35:27.542
Hello?

35:30.837 --> 35:34.215
Oh, I'm so sorry!
This week I'm fully booked.

35:34.298 --> 35:35.633
Excuse me!

35:35.716 --> 35:38.094
Two orders of sundae gukbap
and soju please.

35:38.719 --> 35:39.595
‎Hey!

35:39.679 --> 35:42.306
How are you doing? Having fun?

35:42.390 --> 35:43.683
I'm doing well.

35:43.766 --> 35:46.394
I might be able to apply
for my second visa soon.

35:47.687 --> 35:48.938
Ivanna!

35:50.648 --> 35:52.358
Look, she's my roommate.

36:01.450 --> 36:03.911
Hello. This is Shige.

36:05.580 --> 36:07.248
I don't know what's going on,

36:07.915 --> 36:09.542
but I'm glad to see
that you're doing well.

36:09.625 --> 36:11.252
Yeah. Where's Taiga today?

36:11.335 --> 36:15.423
Oh, he's pretty busy with his other job.

36:16.174 --> 36:17.466
Their game is tomorrow,

36:17.550 --> 36:20.720
so the menu is heavier
on the carbohydrates than usual.

36:21.596 --> 36:24.557
And to boost the athletes' performance,
we chose

36:24.640 --> 36:28.060
ingredients and cooking methods that
promote easier digestion and absorption.

36:32.106 --> 36:33.274
Yes.

36:33.774 --> 36:34.901
This is good, Taiga.

36:35.568 --> 36:37.695
All right, let's go with this.

36:37.778 --> 36:40.031
Okay. Let's start preparing.

36:40.114 --> 36:41.157
-Yes.
-Yes.

36:43.826 --> 36:47.955
MAMA'S SEASONAL MUST-TRY DINER
RED CHILI PASTE BULGOGI

36:48.039 --> 36:53.628
RESTAURANT GARDEN BALAM

36:56.672 --> 36:57.506
Over here!

36:58.090 --> 36:59.842
You're late!

36:59.926 --> 37:00.927
Sorry!

37:01.010 --> 37:02.887
I'm famished. Let's hurry up and order.

37:02.970 --> 37:04.347
What do you feel like?

37:04.430 --> 37:05.973
-I don't know…
-It's hard, huh?

37:08.226 --> 37:10.519
We survived another week.

37:11.103 --> 37:12.647
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

37:17.235 --> 37:18.653
This is the best!

37:19.320 --> 37:22.073
I can feel it bring
my whole body back to life!

37:24.075 --> 37:26.077
This week was crazy, as always.

37:26.160 --> 37:27.954
Me too.

37:28.037 --> 37:31.582
But living a fulfilling life
is a good thing.

37:31.666 --> 37:32.750
True.

37:33.376 --> 37:34.543
Do you enjoy your job?

37:35.670 --> 37:36.712
Yeah.

37:36.796 --> 37:37.755
Please enjoy.

37:37.838 --> 37:39.465
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

37:41.759 --> 37:42.718
This looks good.

37:43.719 --> 37:45.388
You really like that, don't you?

37:47.181 --> 37:49.141
Is it because of your ex-boyfriend?

38:00.861 --> 38:02.238
This is amazing!

38:02.321 --> 38:04.156
This gimbap is so good!

38:04.240 --> 38:05.658
Thank you.

38:05.741 --> 38:07.785
Someone special to me
taught me how to make it.

38:24.260 --> 38:26.637
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION AND ALL CHARACTERS
AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTIONAL

38:26.721 --> 38:28.723
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
